0.3.0 (2026-11-28):
- Edit dialog: new setting "Labels" – descriptions in Polish for a Polish system, English for all others,
  or chosen by hand (English / Polski); only the descriptions change, fields and values stay the same

0.2.0 (2026-11-26):
- New: start from the number in msg.payload (e.g. the current brightness) – GitHub issue #1.
  Option "Start from the number in msg.payload"; the direction follows from it, equal to the stop value = "end" at once;
  text, objects and timestamps (default inject) keep the configured start value
- New: "Time from there" – always the configured time, or the same speed (a shorter range takes less time)

0.1.0 (2026-11-25):
- Fixed: package.json registered the node under the "afya-panic-button" key
  (conflict when both packages were installed)
- New: current state ({ value, state, direction, … }) in a global/flow context variable
- Fixed: timer kept running after a redeploy
- Configuration checked on deploy, errors are passed to a Catch node
- Message properties of the starting message are kept
- New modern edit dialog (sections, live summary, spinners, validation), palette category "AFYA",
  Font Awesome icon, English UI with English + Polish help
- Short, consistent node status (value · time)
- MIT license, Node-RED >= 3.0, Node.js >= 18, unit tests (`npm test`)

0.0.2:
- you can whip a thread if you send a message to him:
msg.payload = "kill" or msg.payload = "stop"
- 'step' option has been added - step, if the value between steps is to change
- the option of counting down has been added. so it's not just a lullaby, but also a function: a nice morning (i.e. slow wake-up call) = counting up
- a security option has been added for those able to otherwise;)


